Accept a pkgbase file inside a package-owned kernel directory

Arch Linux ARM's kernel packages ship no usr/lib/modules/<ver>/pkgbase.
Omarchy's linux-aarch64-pkgbase-shim writes one from a pacman hook, so the
file itself is owned by no package, and limine-mkinitcpio-install skips it.
Treat a pkgbase whose modules directory is owned by a package the same as an
owned pkgbase; a leftover directory of a removed kernel is owned by nothing
and is still skipped.

RETIRE: delete this file and its prepare() line when Arch Linux ARM's
linux-aarch64 ships pkgbase itself (archlinuxarm/PKGBUILDs#2215 or its
successor) and linux-aarch64-pkgbase-shim is dropped.

--- a/install/arch-linux/limine-mkinitcpio-hook/usr/share/libalpm/scripts/limine-mkinitcpio-install
+++ b/install/arch-linux/limine-mkinitcpio-hook/usr/share/libalpm/scripts/limine-mkinitcpio-install
@@ -240,8 +240,10 @@ process_kernel() {
 	local pkgbase_file="$1"
 
 	[[ -f "$pkgbase_file" ]] || return 0
-	# Skip if pkgbase file is not owned by any package
-	pacman -Qqo "$pkgbase_file" &>/dev/null || return 0
+	# Skip if neither the pkgbase file nor its kernel directory is owned by a
+	# package (Arch Linux ARM kernels ship no pkgbase; a hook writes one).
+	pacman -Qqo "$pkgbase_file" &>/dev/null ||
+		pacman -Qqo "${pkgbase_file%/pkgbase}" &>/dev/null || return 0
 	set_kernel_context "$pkgbase_file" || return 0
 
 	if [[ "${ENABLE_UKI:-}" == "yes" ]] && is_uefi; then
